[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) merged every report about wrong dates into one ticket. The reports describe three separate problems with three different fixes, so each one now has its own ticket.

<Callout kind="warn">
The fix queued for #4471 fixes the parser. It does not touch the booking-v3 form hint or time-zone handling,
so those reports keep coming after it ships.
</Callout>

## The split

| Problem | Reports | Issue | Cause |
|---------|---------|-------|-------|
| parser | 379 | [#4](https://github.com/poponuts/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/4) | Date parser reads month-first; day-first tenants' dates swap |
| hint | 33 | [#5](https://github.com/poponuts/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/5) | booking-v3 form hint says MM/DD/YYYY; people type month-first |
| shift | 5 | [#6](https://github.com/poponuts/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/6) | One-day moves; time-zone conversion, not swaps |

## How to tell them apart

- **parser**: A day-first tenant. The day and month in the report swap (7 April became 4 July). The report came by app, by email, or through a booking-v2 form.
- **hint**: The same swap, but through the booking form of a booking-v3 tenant. That form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field, so people type the month first, and the form reads the tenant's way (day-first). Fixing the parser does not fix this one; the form hint has to change.
- **shift**: A few reports describe a one-day move, not a swap ("Lisbon got Tuesday, Toronto got Monday"). The desk reads them as one-day moves and counts them where their cause files them; their ticket is closed as a duplicate.

Read the report body and the tenant, not the intake tag: intake guesses from the reporter's browser, and its tag disagrees with the cause on dozens of reports.

